<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>The eve of all creation</l><l>He mused on His delight,</l><l>And pondered every feature,</l><l>Well-pleasing in His sight.</l><l>Creation sprang to being,</l><l>But deep in Him did hide</l><l>A heart of depth unfathomed</l><l>Fixed on a glorious Bride.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>And thus His will was ’stablished</l><l>His counterpart to gain:</l><l>This blessed, firm intention,</l><l>Eternally the same.</l><l>Though sin should e’en beguile man,</l><l>Then mock his helpless state,</l><l>He never could forsake her,</l><l>His yearning ne’er abate.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Then mercy richly flourished,</l><l>And love was, oh, so vast,</l><l>As graciously He sought her</l><l>With wisdom unsurpassed.</l><l>The love He gave to win her</l><l>God only comprehends!</l><l>His life laid down, an offering</l><l>Whose fragrance yet ascends.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>And now in resurrection</l><l>To her He draws most near,</l><l>And with untold affection</l><l>In glory does appear.</l><l>As she beholds her Bridegroom,</l><l>His glory floods her heart,</l><l>’Til she, His Bride, is raptured,</l><l>His longed-for counterpart.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
